Added. The reason is worth stating because it is not local to this file. Every route into here has already dealt with the stored round. handleShowOrderIntent falls through to the summary request only when parseUnresolvedClarifications came back empty, which after a republish means the menu no longer carries what the round asked about. handleOrderInitiation falls through only when the field is undefined. The pay-link tap and /pagar reach it only on an AwaitingPayment order, and updateOrder deletes the field on that path. So what survives to this write is unaskable, and keeping it would re-send a question about an item the menu dropped.

The comment reads:

// A caller with an answerable question replies with it instead of coming
// here, so a question still stored is one the republished menu cannot ask.

Swept the branch for the pattern. Two production calls pass unresolvedClarifications: undefined and are new on this branch, this one and the repricing write in handleInitiateOrderPayment. Both carry a line now, the pay-tap one saying an order waiting to be paid carries no open question to keep.

Six older calls pass undefined and are untouched by this branch. handleDoneIntent and the two in handleOrderInitiation already say why above the call. The two in handleRepeatOrder and the one in handleOrderText do not. Say the word and I cover them here rather than filing it.
